{"id":170,"flavor":[{"games":["Shield","X","SoulSilver","FireRed","Silver"],"text":"On the dark ocean floor, its only means of communication is its constantly flashing lights."},{"games":["Sword","Crystal"],"text":"Its antennae, which evolved from a fin, have both positive and negative charges flowing through them."},{"games":["Ultra Moon"],"text":"Chinchou blink their shining antennae at one another to claim their respective turf."},{"games":["Ultra Sun"],"text":"Its two antennae glow softly to lure in prey, making it a useful Pokémon for night fishing."},{"games":["Moon"],"text":"It lives in the depths beyond the reach of sunlight. It flashes lights on its antennae to communicate with others of its kind."},{"games":["Sun"],"text":"Its two antennae were originally fins. It discharges electricity to stun its prey before attacking."},{"games":["Alpha Sapphire","Sapphire"],"text":"Chinchou’s two antennas are filled with cells that generate strong electricity. This Pokémon’s cells create so much electrical power, it even makes itself tingle slightly."},{"games":["Omega Ruby","Ruby"],"text":"Chinchou lets loose positive and negative electrical charges from its two antennas to make its prey faint. This Pokémon flashes its electric lights to exchange signals with others."},{"games":["Y","HeartGold","LeafGreen","Gold"],"text":"It shoots positive and negative electricity between the tips of its two antennae and zaps its enemies."},{"games":["White 2","Black 2","White","Black","Platinum","Pearl","Diamond"],"text":"It discharges positive and negative electricity from its antenna tips to shock its foes."},{"games":["Emerald"],"text":"When it senses danger, it discharges positive and negative electricity from its two antennae. It lives in depths beyond sunlight’s reach."}],"abilities":[{"name":"Volt Absorb","hidden":false,"description":"If hit by an Electric-type move, the Pokémon has its HP restored instead of taking damage."},{"name":"Illuminate","hidden":false,"description":